# Trivy ignore file — odoocker-goldberrygrove
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line. Optional `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` suffix sets an
# expiration after which Trivy re-flags the entry, forcing a periodic re-review.
#
# Scope ignores as tightly as possible. Each entry must be justified by a
# comment immediately above it explaining:
#   1. why the CVE doesn't apply (or is mitigated) in our deployment
#   2. the expected fix path (upstream patch, base image rev, removal of dep)
#
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 — PostCSS path traversal in previous-source-map
# auto-loading. postcss 8.5.14 (fixed 8.5.18) ships bundled inside the
# upstream `odoo:19` base image at
#   /usr/local/lib/node_modules/rtlcss/node_modules/postcss
# rtlcss is Odoo's RTL-CSS transformer; it only ever processes Odoo's own
# trusted bundled asset CSS at build/asset-generation time — never
# attacker-controlled input — so the source-map path-traversal is not
# reachable in our deployment. Not our dependency: we cannot bump it without
# an upstream `odoo:19` rebuild that revs rtlcss's postcss. Re-review on
# expiry; drop this entry once a newer odoo:19 base ships postcss ≥ 8.5.18.
# Tracked: GOL-934.
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 exp:2026-09-15
